This comment is not a PR blocker, but a further discussion that can be a follow-up.
So, when I looked at this, I first noticed that it looked like we can cache `minMatchNum` result because we now have a map per constraint. (TpValueToMatchNum)

And, that led me to a further idea, should we pre-calculate and filter a result per topology value per constraint? 
I mean, we now almost pre-calculate all the Filter() results per domain/constraint, why not we don't pre-calculate all like:

```go
type preFilterState struct {
  // ToValueToFilterResult has a pre-calculated filter result. 
  // It's a slice indexed by constraint index, and map is keyed with topology value and valued with the filtering result.
  ToValueToFilterResult []map[string]bool
}

func (pl *PodTopologySpread) Filter(ctx context.Context, cycleState *framework.CycleState, pod *v1.Pod, nodeInfo *framework.NodeInfo) *framework.Status {

...

	for i, c := range s.Constraints {
		tpKey := c.TopologyKey
		tpVal, ok := node.Labels[c.TopologyKey]
		if !ok {
			logger.V(5).Info("Node doesn't have required label", "node", klog.KObj(node), "label", tpKey)
			return framework.NewStatus(framework.UnschedulableAndUnresolvable, ErrReasonNodeLabelNotMatch)
		}

		if !c.ToValueToFilterResult[i][tpVal] {
			return framework.NewStatus(framework.UnschedulableAndUnresolvable, ErrReasonConstraintsNotMatch)
		}
	}

	return nil
}
```

What do you think?
